● Yes — two real simplifications, ranked by payoff.

  Big win: replace StandaloneHelperSafe with a denotational premise. The helper's body is already constrained to noCall ∧ heapFree ∧ forkFree, which is almost exactly PureStmt. If the premise is "h.body is denoted by some f : List Val → Val, and ∀
  vs, helper_post vs (f vs)" (delivered by the existing Machine.denote_iff and PureHelperBridge), three things collapse at once:
  - body_deterministic is free — denotation is a function.
  - The InBody arm pins v_h = f vs deterministically; the case-4 .ret alignment becomes a denote_iff invocation.
  - helper_value_exists becomes ⟨f vs, h_spec vs _⟩.

  This trades an operational obligation (which the last agent got stuck on) for a denotational one (which already has all the infrastructure). The procs-table-irrelevance and assignAllParams ↔ bindParams gaps also shrink because the denotational
  side runs from a fixed env. Drops the file by maybe 200-300 LoC and eliminates the three missing lemmas.

  Cheap win: require helper_post functional in vs. Add ∀ v v', helper_post vs v → helper_post vs v' → v = v' as a side condition. Kills body_deterministic without restructuring anything. Doesn't fix the env-alignment or procs-irrelevance gaps. Most
   realistic specs (fun vs v ↔ v = f vs) satisfy it trivially. ~30 LoC of statement changes; simulation_step case 4 becomes routine.

  Cosmetic: drop reducibility from the InBody arm. Re-derive on demand in sim_transfer (the only consumer). One field gone, one preservation obligation gone, but it doesn't change the difficulty class of simulation_step — case 3 still needs to
  argue body steps progress.

  Cosmetic: move/delete the smoke test. Its two sorrys look like real holes and aren't. Confusing.

  Verdict. The denotational approach is the right simplification. The current operational forward-simulation is a faithful translation of the paper-style argument but fights against existing infrastructure — Agar already has denote_iff proving
  exactly the determinism + trajectory-alignment facts the simulation argument keeps re-asserting. The previous attempt got stuck precisely on the operational facts that the denotational layer hands you for free.

  The functional-helper_post route is a smaller, safer simplification if you want to keep the operational flavor and not refactor toward PureStmt. Either is strictly better than the current path.

