  Specifically: replace h.body.heapFree ∧ h.body.forkFree ∧ h.body.noCall (three predicates whose interaction has to be re-derived everywhere) with a structural assumption h.body = embed pureBody ; .ret retExpr for some pureBody : PureStmt. Then:

  1. One big-step lemma carries the whole helper body. Prove helper_runs_to_value: from ⟨h.body, [], bindParams h.params vs, frame :: rest, none⟩, the concrete machine deterministically reaches ⟨.skip, frame.cont, frame.env.set frame.rv v, rest,
